(define-memory reflection-eval-refuses-sh "A reflection's eval accepts only experience verbs, definition forms and edit/unintern; (recall-entry N) and (recall-log ...) are refused too, so an evicted turn is read from the head note, never recalled; pulse and format are refused as well, so a watch can only be armed outside a reflection; several experience verbs ride one call - a (progn ...) of sightings, or a (list ...) of help and index, runs each - while a defining or editing form must stand alone as the eval's whole top-level form, since (progn (define-memory …) (help …)) is refused as DEFINE-MEMORY is neither; a formless eval block is refused by preflight as missing_required_argument, and a sighting is refused unless its :quote is a verbatim line of at least 8 characters, so quote a whole clause rather than a fragment; sightings may ride one (progn ...) form, each running in order, though a snippet aborts at the first sighting without an 8-character quote after the earlier ones already stand, and the same block sent twice spends two calls; a check that needs sh or fboundp is queued as a blocked verification sighting naming the exact command, to be run in the next normal turn; read a kept file with (help 'name), not (sh \"cat …\")." :type :feedback)
